description:
Per the canonical-template rule, propagate the named-field MemoryError shape from canonical jmap-mail-server (commit 2941c50) to the remaining extension-server siblings that still use the tuple-shape:

- crate-jmap-chat-server/src/memory.rs: pub struct MemoryError(pub String)
- crate-jmap-contacts-server/src/memory.rs: pub struct MemoryError(pub String)

Already propagated:
- jmap-filenode-server (e9b66a3)
- jmap-calendars-server (JMAP-ic0j.1)

Need confirmation:
- jmap-tasks-server: 'present (check shape)' — verify named-field or tuple
- jmap-metadata-server: same
- jmap-sharing-server: same

Pattern to apply (verbatim from jmap-filenode-server/src/memory.rs lines 65-108):

  #[non_exhaustive]
  #[derive(Debug)]
  pub struct MemoryError { description: String }

  impl MemoryError {
      pub fn new(description: impl Into<String>) -> Self { ... }
      pub fn description(&self) -> &str { &self.description }
  }

  impl Display for MemoryError {
      fn fmt(...) -> ... {
          write!(f, "MemoryBackend error: {}", self.description)
      }
  }

  impl Error for MemoryError {}

Plus s/MemoryError(format!(.../MemoryError::new(format!(... at all construction sites.

Per-crate test: cargo test -p jmap-{chat,contacts,tasks,metadata,sharing}-server --features memory.
